    historyContent: {
      origins: 'The Tarocco Bolognese is one of the oldest tarot decks in continual use. Tarocchi were mentioned in connection with Bologna by 1442 and in Bologna itself by 1459. The deck was reduced from 78 to 62 cards during the 16th century by removing ranks 2 to 5 from each suit; in 1725 the imperial and papal trumps were converted to four Moors. The deck and its games have historically been confined to Bologna.',
